  message: "[Wave-0 hygiene re-verify] Rescope WI-totak to track THREE no-fix ignores (not two): CVE-2025-69872 (diskcache via llama_cpp_python), PYSEC-2026-139 (torch), and CVE-2025-3000 (torch advisory family variant, added 2026-06-10). Distinguish from two permanent CI ignores: CVE-2025-71176 (pytest dev-only) and CVE-2026-3219 (pip AV:L). Action: at each release or when this item surfaces in `tracker ready`, run pip-audit -f json and for each of the three, if a fixed version exists, upgrade the package and remove the corresponding --ignore-vuln flag + comment block from scripts/release-check:212-227. Close only when all three no-fix ignores are removed. Reference: scripts/release-check:202-227."  # 8c43
- op: discuss  # 789d
  at: '2026-08-18T06:23:20Z'  # 789d
  by: agent  # 789d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 789d
  clock: 3  # 789d
  nonce: 789d  # 789d
  message: "RE-CHECKED BOTH IGNORES 2026-08-18 WITH LIVE RUNS, not by re-reading the list.\nThis is what this item asked for; one of the two is now discharged.\n\nPYSEC-2026-597 (nltk) -- DROPPED in PR #407. It was carried as \"no fix\navailable\" and that had stopped being true: nltk 3.10 fixes it along with\nPYSEC-2026-3582/3583/3584. Evidence: with the ignore removed and nltk upgraded,\npip-audit reports \"No known vulnerabilities found, 6 ignored\". nltk is now\nPINNED in the local audit-env sync instead, per the script's own policy that\nfixable deps are pinned rather than ignored. A dead ignore in a security gate is\nworse than the advisory it names -- it is a false statement about what was\nchecked, and it suppresses the NEXT advisory for that package.\n\nCVE-2025-69872 (diskcache) -- STAYS, and this was tested rather than assumed.\nDropping it does not produce a clean audit: it surfaces PYSEC-2026-2447, which\nis the same advisory under its PYSEC id (pip-audit resolves the alias, which is\nwhy only one of the two ids ever appears), and it STILL has no fix version.\ndiskcache reaches this box via CairoSVG/safety and is not a dependency of any\nshipped hypergumbo package.\n\nTHE ITEM STAYS OPEN because its trigger is still live for the remaining\ncarve-out: when diskcache ships a fix, the ignore should be dropped and the dep\npinned. The comment block in release-check now records both results inline, so a\nfuture reader does not have to re-derive them."  # 789d
